WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.239
One child. Two changes in one gene, BUB1B. It makes the
protein that checks chromosomes are shared out correctly when
a cell divides.

2
00:00:11.414 --> 00:00:34.197
No approved medicine acts on that protein. So every candidate
acts on a consequence instead. And no repurposed drug has ever
been given to anyone with this syndrome, for the syndrome.
Nothing in this work is expected to reduce this child's cancer
risk. That is on the first page of the report, and it is said
here.

3
00:00:34.372 --> 00:00:48.563
So the question changed. How do you search honestly when the
answer is probably no? Two expert panels worked on the same
five dossiers, blind to each other. Thirteen seats.

4
00:00:48.738 --> 00:01:10.681
Then ten divergent files, written without access to either
panel. Then verification: every claim the arguments actually
turned on, checked against the primary source. Then three
independent referees. No seat could defer to the other panel,
because no seat knew what it had written. This was built to
find its own errors.

5
00:01:10.856 --> 00:01:17.295
It found them. The two candidates that looked best did not
survive.

6
00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:34.853
Metformin fails on exposure. The concentration that did
something in a dish is thirty two to a hundred and thirty fold
above what a child reaches. Dose cannot close that gap. The
ceiling is lactic acidosis.

7
00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:46.915
Senolytic therapy fails on three independent grounds. Any one
of them is enough. There is no paediatric senolytic dose in
any condition.

8
00:01:47.090 --> 00:02:07.929
Verification caught a survival figure that was wrong, sitting
inside the clause written to stop cancer treatment being
withheld. And a supporting allele turned out to be a splice
variant, not a nonsense variant. It could not support the
readthrough argument at all. Both corrections are printed in
the report.

9
00:02:08.104 --> 00:02:25.295
What survives is smaller. First, a list of ordinary medicines
to avoid, with a carve-out that protects cancer treatment. It
is written by intent, not as a closed list, so it cannot be
read as a reason to change a chemotherapy plan.

10
00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:38.893
Second, four additions to surveillance at no cost. One of them
reads UGT1A1, the irinotecan safety marker, out of data that
has already been sequenced.

11
00:02:39.068 --> 00:02:55.851
Third, a kidney work-up before any kidney drug, because two
causes are possible and they need opposite treatments. Fourth,
a measurement gate. Its first item returns a number that
exists for no patient with this syndrome.

12
00:02:56.026 --> 00:03:21.905
The method transfers. Change the gene and the tool runs again:
it queried a hundred and ten targets and returned twenty nine
approved drugs in under six minutes. The gate is the part
worth copying. What is not known: whether the two changes sit
on separate copies, how much protein this child makes, whether
the target is there at all. The report says so.

13
00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:26.580
Track 2. A hypothesis for follow-up.
Not evidence that a medicine works.
